Vulkan encode: recover from lost frames without a keyframe

When the caller sets the frame metadata "hw_encode_invalidate_refs" to the
pts of the first picture the decoder lost, the next picture references the
newest picture before it instead of the lost ones (a P-picture, not an IDR).
Moonlight calls this reference frame invalidation.

To keep such a picture available, the "ref_history" option (H.265 and AV1)
keeps up to that many reference pictures in the DPB: the two newest and,
further back, every fourth one. The H.265 RPS lists them as unused by the
current picture, and the VPS/SPS DPB size and level account for them. AV1
pictures take the lowest free reference slot instead of ping-ponging between
slots 0 and 1, so the history keeps its slots. If no picture before the loss
is left, or ref_history is 0 (and always for H.264), the picture becomes an
IDR as before.

